issues.body:
### Describe the bug

DataFusion is meant to skip validating spill files when it reads them back, because it wrote them itself (#15454). Since #21882 (55.0.0), `SpillReaderStream` reads them with `StreamDecoder::with_skip_validation(true)` ([mod.rs#L337-L339](https://github.com/apache/datafusion/blob/c6869995c11c0e6661106f9d188dede8672ecc69/datafusion/physical-plan/src/spill/mod.rs#L337-L339)). But arrow-ipc's `StreamDecoder` only passes that flag to dictionary batches ([stream.rs#L247-L277](https://github.com/apache/arrow-rs/blob/df4dc3ede59bd43b5f71847231212381d068bb72/arrow-ipc/src/reader/stream.rs#L247-L277)). Every spilled record batch is validated again, including a UTF-8 check of every string.

### To Reproduce

A spilled `Utf8` value that is not UTF-8 fails to read back:

```rust
let binary = BinaryArray::from_iter_values([b"\xa0\xa1".as_slice(), b"valid"]);
let strings = unsafe {
    StringArray::new_unchecked(binary.offsets().clone(), binary.values().clone(), None)
};
let batch = RecordBatch::try_from_iter([("s", Arc::new(strings) as ArrayRef)])?;
let spill_file = spill_manager
    .spill_record_batch_and_finish(&[batch], "Test")?
    .unwrap();
collect(spill_manager.read_spill_as_stream(spill_file, None)?).await?;
// Invalid argument error: Invalid UTF8 sequence at string index 0 (0..2): invalid utf-8 sequence of 1 bytes from index 0
```

### Expected behavior

Spilled batches read back without validation, as before 55.0.0. In the `spill_io` benchmark, reading 100 spilled batches of 8192 rows with a `Utf8` column takes 9.4 ms on main and 8.2 ms without validation.

### Additional context

arrow-ipc 56.1 through 60.0 and arrow-rs main have the same `StreamDecoder` code. arrow-ipc tests `skip_validation` with `StreamReader`, `FileReader` and `FileDecoder`, but not with `StreamDecoder`. Found while working on #26627.

### Willingness to contribute

I plan to contribute a fix for this bug independently
